1
00:00:00,690 --> 00:00:03,968
So we're making good progress here with this

2
00:00:03,968 --> 00:00:06,522
demo app and we'll soon switch to another

3
00:00:06,763 --> 00:00:09,526
demo app. But before we do that, there's one

4
00:00:09,815 --> 00:00:12,627
other HTMX feature you should know about

5
00:00:12,627 --> 00:00:15,438
because it can further simplify your code

6
00:00:15,438 --> 00:00:17,912
and come in handy in certain situations.

7
00:00:19,406 --> 00:00:22,426
Some of these attributes like hx-target, for

8
00:00:22,426 --> 00:00:24,611
example, but also hx-swap

9
00:00:25,157 --> 00:00:28,674
accept extra code. Configuration settings,

10
00:00:28,947 --> 00:00:29,460
you could say.

11
00:00:30,375 --> 00:00:32,685
And we'll take a look at the extra settings

12
00:00:32,878 --> 00:00:36,488
you can make to hx-swap a little bit later.

13
00:00:36,553 --> 00:00:39,056
For the moment, I wanna focus on hx-target

14
00:00:39,056 --> 00:00:39,473
instead.

15
00:00:40,725 --> 00:00:43,934
Because hx-target, as you learned, takes

16
00:00:43,934 --> 00:00:47,801
such a CSS selector to select the target

17
00:00:47,865 --> 00:00:50,208
element in the currently active page, in the

18
00:00:50,208 --> 00:00:51,459
currently rendered DOM

19
00:00:52,037 --> 00:00:54,364
that should be replaced with the response

20
00:00:54,364 --> 00:00:54,701
content.

21
00:00:55,748 --> 00:00:57,910
However, what's important to note here

22
00:00:58,491 --> 00:01:00,976
is that you're not limited to specifying

23
00:01:01,008 --> 00:01:02,654
such a CSS selector.

24
00:01:03,364 --> 00:01:05,813
It might be what you do in most scenarios,

25
00:01:06,247 --> 00:01:08,111
but it's not the only thing you can do.

26
00:01:09,621 --> 00:01:12,048
Instead, you can, for example, also use the

27
00:01:12,048 --> 00:01:15,412
special this keyword here as a value for

28
00:01:15,493 --> 00:01:16,269
hx-target.

29
00:01:17,514 --> 00:01:19,099
And this simply tells

30
00:01:19,681 --> 00:01:20,522
HTMX

31
00:01:21,055 --> 00:01:22,494
that it's the element on which this

32
00:01:22,672 --> 00:01:26,035
attribute was placed that should be replaced

33
00:01:26,067 --> 00:01:27,584
with the response content.

34
00:01:28,633 --> 00:01:31,198
And that actually is the default of

35
00:01:31,295 --> 00:01:33,957
HX-Target, so you typically don't need to

36
00:01:33,957 --> 00:01:34,620
set that.

37
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:38,418
You could just omit HX-Target instead, but

38
00:01:38,434 --> 00:01:40,277
nonetheless, it's worth knowing about this.

39
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,989
More useful is another variation of this

40
00:01:46,054 --> 00:01:47,768
HX-Target value though,

41
00:01:48,319 --> 00:01:50,988
because you can actually also use some

42
00:01:51,069 --> 00:01:53,323
commands here in HX-Target. And that's a

43
00:01:53,323 --> 00:01:54,110
feature that will come in handy

44
00:01:56,754 --> 00:01:59,532
with the hx-target usage on this remove

45
00:01:59,628 --> 00:01:59,933
button.

46
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:03,659
Because here I'm targeting the list item

47
00:02:03,675 --> 00:02:06,565
that should be removed with the ID, so with

48
00:02:06,774 --> 00:02:09,889
this ID that was assigned to the list item.

49
00:02:11,029 --> 00:02:14,176
Now that works, but we could also use the

50
00:02:14,722 --> 00:02:19,587
closest command and then use a simpler CSS

51
00:02:19,652 --> 00:02:23,329
selector like the list item tag selector to

52
00:02:23,329 --> 00:02:28,071
target the closest list item seen relative

53
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:29,206
from this button.

54
00:02:31,357 --> 00:02:33,680
If we would just use list item, we would

55
00:02:33,696 --> 00:02:36,439
select the first list item on the entire

56
00:02:36,439 --> 00:02:39,713
page, which is not necessarily the list item

57
00:02:39,762 --> 00:02:42,250
we wanna delete. But if we use the closest

58
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:45,889
command in front of this CSS selector, we

59
00:02:46,051 --> 00:02:48,380
actually select the closest list item

60
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,095
relative from this button.

61
00:02:51,249 --> 00:02:53,271
And this doesn't have to be a tag selector

62
00:02:53,271 --> 00:02:54,765
here. This could be anything,

63
00:02:55,583 --> 00:02:56,274
also some

64
00:02:56,868 --> 00:02:57,606
ID selector.

65
00:02:58,971 --> 00:03:02,230
But by using closest li, we now actually no

66
00:03:02,326 --> 00:03:04,750
longer need to assign such an ID to this

67
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:07,367
list item and we can get rid of that code

68
00:03:07,399 --> 00:03:07,817
therefore.

69
00:03:08,748 --> 00:03:12,007
And hence we overall simplified this HTML

70
00:03:12,055 --> 00:03:12,344
code.

71
00:03:13,564 --> 00:03:16,197
And closest isn't the only command you can

72
00:03:16,213 --> 00:03:18,269
use here. If you take a look at the

73
00:03:18,398 --> 00:03:20,132
hx-target documentation,

74
00:03:20,710 --> 00:03:23,570
you see that you could also use find in

75
00:03:23,618 --> 00:03:26,525
front of a CSS selector, for example, to

76
00:03:26,894 --> 00:03:30,171
find a child element, the first child

77
00:03:30,267 --> 00:03:33,560
element with that CSS selector inside of the

78
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:36,194
element on which the hx-target attribute was

79
00:03:36,371 --> 00:03:36,628
placed.

80
00:03:37,576 --> 00:03:39,808
You could also just use the next command

81
00:03:40,322 --> 00:03:43,629
without any CSS selector to simply select

82
00:03:43,629 --> 00:03:46,979
the next sibling after the element on which

83
00:03:47,123 --> 00:03:50,650
hx-target was placed and so on. So you have

84
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:54,032
these extra commands, closest, find, next,

85
00:03:54,176 --> 00:03:57,798
and so on to control which exact element

86
00:03:57,798 --> 00:04:00,219
should be selected. And this sometimes

87
00:04:00,267 --> 00:04:02,014
allows you to write simpler code

88
00:04:02,607 --> 00:04:04,659
than you would have to write without these

89
00:04:04,691 --> 00:04:07,945
commands. Like here where we were able to

90
00:04:07,961 --> 00:04:10,477
get rid of that unnecessary goal ID in the

91
00:04:10,525 --> 00:04:10,621
end.

92
00:04:12,290 --> 00:04:14,601
And therefore here, if we save these

93
00:04:14,858 --> 00:04:15,243
changes,

94
00:04:16,062 --> 00:04:18,549
I can still click remove and it's still the

95
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:19,978
right item that is removed,

96
00:04:20,571 --> 00:04:22,866
but now we actually achieved that with

97
00:04:23,059 --> 00:04:24,712
leaner and simpler code.
